+# SEMANTIC GUARD, FUTURE-GUARD VARIANT (analysis/semantic_guard/, not upstream
+# vLLM, not part of Xia et al.'s taxonomy). Third sibling of
+# spec_casc_tok_semantic_guard (override) and spec_casc_tok_semantic_guard_and
+# -- different trigger shape entirely: those two gate verification AT the
+# hesitation-marker token itself; this one gates the K positions AFTER
+# spec-casc-tok's own relaxed test accepts one, on the theory (see
+# analysis/semantic_guard/README.md's mechanism section) that a hesitation/
+# discourse marker signals a decision fork in the model's own reasoning, and
+# the risk isn't necessarily the marker token itself so much as what gets
+# built on top of it in the next few tokens.
